Included and adapted with permission confirmed by Anima's maintainer on
2026-10-11. Upstream declares no public license for this artwork/font. It is
separate from Anima's Apache-2.0 implementation; no broader font license is
asserted here. Upstream's MIT tokenizer notice does not license this artwork.
No tokenizer, token text, song material or upstream rendering code is included.

accelerando-terminal.ttf is the Accelerando Terminal Regular derivative.
Glyph ID i maps to U+100000+i (8192 entries, through U+101FFF), avoiding the
supplementary-A range used by Nerd Fonts. Outlines retain their orientation
and topology. The affine transform x'=0.6x, y'=1.2y-211.2 fits a 600-unit mono
advance and raises glyph height to ordinary Matrix capitals, at 1000 units/em.
The family name is distinct from the upstream square-advance font.
